Bulmaca — data sources and licences

puzzles.txt (400 crosswords, 11×11) was generated by tools/bulmaca/build-puzzles.py from tools/bulmaca/words.tsv,
which tools/bulmaca/build-words.py built on 2026-10-19 from:

1. Turkish Wiktionary (Vikisözlük, https://tr.wiktionary.org), text under CC BY-SA 4.0
   (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), in the machine-readable extraction published by kaikki.org:
     https://kaikki.org/trwiktionary/raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl.gz
     extracted 2026-10-19 from the trwiktionary dump dated 2026-10-02 with wiktextract 05f0d93 /
     wikitextprocessor 04e9833 (Tatu Ylonen, "Wiktextract: Wiktionary as Machine-Readable Structured Data",
     LREC 2022); downloaded 2026-10-19,
     sha256 19d084d54d21662fba8ffb84090747265ce57c68f0d256a156e81fc68ccadc42 (45 899 849 bytes)
   Used: Turkish lemmas (nouns, adjectives, adverbs, verbs) and a short definition of each, which becomes the clue.
   Clues are shortened (parentheses removed, the first of several definitions, leading synonyms of a list) and
   capitalised; otherwise they are Wiktionary's wording. Senses that are form-of, dialectal, obsolete, slang,
   vulgar or offensive, and senses that mention or cite TDK, were skipped. Nothing was taken from the TDK
   (Türk Dil Kurumu) dictionaries or website: Wiktionary text is the only source of clues.

2. hermitdave/FrequencyWords, Turkish 50k list (CC BY-SA 4.0):
     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords/525f9b560de45753a5ea01069454e72e9aa541c6/content/2018/tr/tr_50k.txt
     sha256 480192844e7fdfe9591bbf0b9cfbb96ed5751cfbba7024fd45d8cb7508e07d5c
   Used only to keep common words (frequency rank < 20 000).

Because both sources are CC BY-SA 4.0, tools/bulmaca/words.tsv and puzzles.txt are distributed under
CC BY-SA 4.0 (attribution: Vikisözlük contributors; Hermit Dave, FrequencyWords). The puzzle layouts are
original (generated). kaikki.org replaces its file with a newer extraction about once a week, so the committed
words.tsv is the reproducible input: `tools/bulmaca/build-puzzles.py` regenerates puzzles.txt byte for byte.

Family-friendly filtering: words with any vulgar/offensive/slang sense or with sexual, crime, violence, death,
religion or drug topics are dropped, as is every answer or clue containing a word of the blocklist in
build-words.py. Clues never contain the answer or a word starting with its stem.
